 not a grade-specific measured property.","type":"Manufacturer statement","at":"Moisture","reads":"unread"}]}],"guide":null,"resin":{"polymer":"PVB","exposures":[{"meaning":"Organic solvent resistance","items":[{"agent":"Organic solvents (ethanol, toluene)","verdict":"not-resistant","text":"Mowital grades are soluble in a broad variety of organic solvents... Mowital can be dissolved in single solvents. To obtain low solution viscosities it is recommended to dissolve Mowital in solvent mixtures (e.g. 1:1 mixture of ethanol and toluene)... Mowital HH grades show the highest water resistance and best solubility in non-polar solvents such as toluene.","source":"R-KURARAY-MOWITAL-B-TDS","id":"PB00351","conditions":"Solution preparation at ambient temperature","note":"The reference reports dissolution; \"soluble\" is reserved for water, so recorded as not-resistant.","at":"p. 2 Characteristics; p. 3 Preparation of solutions","screens":true}],"category":"organic-solvent","verdict":"not-resistant","screens":true},{"meaning":"Water solubility","items":[{"agent":"Water","verdict":"resistant","text":"Mowital is not soluble in water. However, a water content of up to 10 % in the solvent mixture is possible and can be used to influence solution viscosity. Water resistance and solubility in non-polar solvents mainly depend on the degree of acetalisation.","source":"R-KURARAY-MOWITAL-B-TDS","id":"PB00352","conditions":null,"note":null,"at":"p. 3 Preparation of solutions; p. 2 Characteristics","screens":false}],"category":"water-solubility","verdict":"resistant","screens":false},{"meaning":"UV and outdoor","items":[{"agent":"Light","verdict":"resistant","text":"Mowital films are resistant to light and heat-sealable at temperatures above 120 °C.","source":"R-KURARAY-MOWITAL-B-TDS","id":"PB00353","conditions":null,"note":"A light-resistance statement for films; no outdoor weathering test is described.","at":"p. 2 Characteristics","screens":false}],"category":"uv-outdoor","verdict":"r